{
  "abstract": "Eliminating the global reverse-depth sweep of backpropagation is a central goal in neuromorphic computing, but conventional forward perturbation rules incur estimator variance scaling with parameter count O(|Theta|/K) or hidden width O(M/K). Adapting Stephen Chung's Weight Maximization and Sylvester-Hadamard exploration, we investigate parameter-space column contraction over an S-token micro-horizon (WM-S and Co-WM-S). Under fixed downstream targets, column isolation replaces sibling-neuron cross-talk with S-token cross-talk, and sampling K distinct Hadamard columns reduces conditional variance by (S-K)/(K(S-1)), vanishing at K=S. We derive exact conditional weight-gradient covariances and counterexamples showing that width invariance requires non-cancellation and support alignment. Throughout this work, we strictly separate strict no-backward methods (zero reverse-depth sweeps and zero local reverse pullbacks) from reverse-depth-free local-reverse-credit controls (bwd_calls=0, retaining block-local reverse pullbacks). First, we establish a two-stage faithful baseline of published DUST: Stage 1 confirms bit-for-bit gradient equivalence (max_grad_diff=0.0) between hook reruns and prefix-cached suffix execution (1.75x speedup) and reproduces 8-layer reference learning (5.8565 vs 5.7486 test nats at P=256); Stage 2 evaluates faithful DUST on ClimbMix d6 (8.192M tokens), reaching 2.37697+/-0.06975 holdout BPB under SGD (P=64), 2.24921+/-0.00044 under Muon (P=64), and 2.10883+/-0.00138 at P=256. Second, we introduce Delayed / Eligibility-Trace Coordinated Weight Maximization (Delayed-Trace-Co-WM-S), a strict no-backward eligibility-trace rule without direct hidden (mlp.c_fc) forward passes or local reverse pullbacks. Across M in {256..4096} at D=256, 34-draw DUST's mlp.c_fc cosine drops 4.43x on synthetic states (0.3060 to 0.0691) and 3.82x on 50-step ClimbMix states (0.2578 to 0.0675), whereas Delayed-Trace-Co-WM-S stays bounded (0.3031 to 0.2582 and 0.2078 to 0.1884), beats dust_faithful_muon_P64 on 200-step multi-width pretraining at D in {128,384,512} under 1-step delay (d1), runs 1.48x faster at P=256 (1534.8 vs 2271.0 ms/step, 2.14471+/-0.00464 BPB), and wins the uninterrupted matched-wall-clock comparison with full LR cooldown (2.22478+/-0.01313 vs 2.24958+/-0.00005 holdout BPB at ~304s). Checkpointed backpropagation retains superior efficiency (1.45179 BPB, 33.3 ms).",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Revision for version 4 addressing all reviewer items from sjX53jD8FnudBvH1 alongside the full v4 update: (1) Added dedicated uninterrupted 2-seed matched-wall-clock comparisons with explicit LR cooldown and holdout BPB evaluation (`matched_wallclock_307s` in `dust_and_delayed_trace_1000steps_d6.json` and Table 9: `delayed_trace_cowm_P256_fast_d1_wc307s` at 200 steps / `303.70+/-0.14s` timed total reaches `2.22478+/-0.01313` holdout BPB, outperforming `dust_faithful_muon_P256_wc308s_144steps` at 144 steps / `303.85+/-0.07s` timed total `2.24958+/-0.00005` by `-0.02481` BPB and `dust_faithful_muon_P256_wc307s` at 135 steps `2.25763+/-0.00021` by `-0.03285` BPB), fixed checkpoint persistence to save and restore `cum_train_s` and `delayed_mlp_buffer`, and documented `total_timed_step_s` across all 1000-step runs; (2) Re-generated `dust_and_delayed_trace_width_diagnostic.json` and Table 7 with exact JSON alignment across Panel A (15-step synthetic state) and Panel B (50-step ClimbMix language-model states evaluated on held-out ClimbMix tokens), adding `dust_direct_hidden_fc_16draws` and decomposing `rel_var_to_mean`, `rel_var_raw_to_ref`, and projection-rescaled `rel_var`; (3) Aligned the Section 2.6 `Delayed-Trace-Co-WM-S` derivation and Gate 2L (`verify_and_diagnose_scaling.py`) with the executable single-sensitivity update (`d_{g,s,i}` inside `tilde{h}`, pre-synaptic input trace `e_g^{(m)} = sum_s xi_{g,s}^{(m)} x_{g,s}`); and (4) Bundled the complete pinned `literature/dust/` repository snapshot (`dust.py`, `model.py`, `prepare_data.py`, `requirements.txt`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`, `baselines/`, `tokenizer/`), corrected the Stage 1A P=256 text reference, and added discussion of concurrent `general_pretraining_19/v1` [13].",
